## Compilation Instructions
To compile all programs, navigate to the project root directory and run:
```bash
make all
```

This will compile all 9 tasks using the provided Makefile with the following flags:
- `-std=c11 -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -pedantic` for C compilation
- `-lpthread` for Task 9 (threading)

## Time Information from Task 10 Performance Analysis
Based on benchmarking results:
- Sequential (Task 1): 0.023s baseline
- Pipe-based (Task 4): 0.009s (2.5x faster)
- Parallel Fork (Task 5): 0.014s (1.6x faster)
- Thread-based (Task 9): 0.025s (slightly slower due to overhead)

## Testing Instructions
1. Test basic compression/decompression:
   ```bash
   cd task_1 && ./MyCompress sample.txt test.cmp && cd ../task_2 && ./MyDecompress ../task_1/test.cmp restored.txt && diff ../task_1/sample.txt restored.txt
   ```

2. Test process management:
   ```bash
   cd task_3 && ./ForkCompress sample_fork.txt fork_test.cmp
   ```

3. Test inter-process communication:
   ```bash
   cd task_4 && ./PipeCompress ../task_1/sample.txt pipe_test.cmp
   ```

4. Test parallel processing:
   ```bash
   cd task_5 && ./ParFork 2 ../task_10/large_test.txt parfork_test.cmp
   ```

5. Test multithreading:
   ```bash
   cd task_9 && ./ParThread 4 ../task_10/large_test.txt thread_test.cmp
   ```

